e1000: disable EEE on a CE4100 PHY under phylink

The MAC has no LPI support. phylink only disables EEE in a PHY when the
MAC implements the LPI operations, so the PHY keeps its default EEE
advertisement. With EEE negotiated, an RTL8211E blinks its link LED about
once a second while the link idles, and a link LED offloaded to the PHY
no longer shows the link state.

Implement the LPI operations with no LPI capabilities, so that phylink
disables EEE in the PHY.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
index 3f6f678..fa66751 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
@@ -1053,10 +1053,26 @@ static void e1000_mac_link_up(struct phylink_config *config,
 	mutex_unlock(&adapter->phylink_lock);
 }
 
+/* The MAC has no LPI. LPI operations with no LPI capabilities tell
+ * phylink so, and it disables EEE in the PHY.
+ */
+static void e1000_mac_disable_tx_lpi(struct phylink_config *config)
+{
+}
+
+static int e1000_mac_enable_tx_lpi(struct phylink_config *config, u32 timer,
+				   bool tx_clk_stop)
+{
+	/* Never called: no LPI capabilities */
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct phylink_mac_ops e1000_phylink_mac_ops = {
 	.mac_config = e1000_mac_config,
 	.mac_link_down = e1000_mac_link_down,
 	.mac_link_up = e1000_mac_link_up,
+	.mac_disable_tx_lpi = e1000_mac_disable_tx_lpi,
+	.mac_enable_tx_lpi = e1000_mac_enable_tx_lpi,
 };
 
 /**
